  overall trump maintains his primacy in  the party in a hypothetical matchup  against five other republican  presidential rivals 49 of primary voters  say they would support him for a third  nomination so we're going to d we're  going to get more into that in a moment  but here are uh some of these  interesting numbers so if a republican  2024 primary were held today who would  you vote for 49 say donald trump  51 say someone else but as you can see  no individual alternative  gets more than 25 percent and that to a  great degree  tells us a lot about the potential  dynamics of a very fractured 2024  republican primary and we are going to  get to that now some interesting um  demographic numbers  um trump does much better significantly  better notably better with men rather  than women 52 versus 45  and trump does significantly better with  those who have no college degree in fact  among those with a college degree trump  loses to desantis 32 to 28 but among  those with no college degree trump more  than doubles ron desantis 58 to 21.  those are  extraordinarily  notable and interesting numbers now one  other aspect to this  is that desantis has not run for  president before  um and so when you look at you know  is polling roughly seven percent in in  this particular poll mike pence is  polling between  five and ten depending on which  demographic group these are known  entities desantis is not as known and in  fact a quarter of republicans said they  don't even have an opinion of desantis  yet because they don't know enough about  him those who know who desantis is  really like him unfortunately a quarter  don't but that's actually a really good  thing for ron desantis because it  suggests at least that theoretically  that as more republicans come to know  desantis  he may be influential uh in getting  people over to his side and later in  today's show we have a voicemail that  asks sort of an important question about  desantis versus trump uh should desantis  and trump face off in a primary  the poll suggested that support from fox  news could prove crucial and this could  be you know i think it is fair to say  that at this point fox news has been  weakened from uh its prior strength  and it has in part been weakened because  of competitors like newsmax and others  it's in part been weakened because  donald trump has been uh significantly  antagonistic to fox news over the last  year and a half  but uh trump holds a 62 to 26 advantage  over desantis among fox news viewers  but among floridians it's 16 points  closer if they use a different primary  source of news if you don't watch fox  you're much less likely to support trump  over the desantis and that would be uh a  really a really critical thing so half  of republicans again with all of these  things you can look at it glass half  full or glass half empty depending on  who you are  one perspective would be  half of republicans  want someone other than trump that's not  particularly good for a former president  on the other hand  trump doubles every other potential  competitor right now  and would easily win a primary if it  were to be held today  uh and you can  decide for yourself which of those two  perspectives is more relevant or more  valid and um that is the new york times  poll  let's now go and talk about what the  primary dynamics could be  i never have time to read all of the  non-fiction books that i want to read  our sponsor blinkist has solved the  problem for me in a way because blinkist  takes thousands of the best and newest  nonfiction books extracts the key  takeaways and then you can either read  or listen to them in 15 minutes i read  all the time i love narrative nonfiction  i read economics i read all these  different things as i said before i  would love to have time to read more  history i just don't right now  especially with a newborn you should see  what's going on in the middle of the  night but  uh with blinkist i was able to read in  fact i